You may count whatever you want :-).  I think *not* wishing can make 
life very hard, depending on the RNG.  Not polypiling without not 
wishing is also a conduct that I don't consider noteworthy.  It becomes 
interesting only in combination with wishless.  Not genociding is 
noteworthy because of the MF and MMF, but it is not difficult either.

> So you declare that a non-conduct and wish for artifacts as you like?

As I said in another post I don't care for conducts.  (This may change, 
because ordinary ascensions may become too easy for me.)  I also 
explained my general attitude towards wishing for artifacts, so no need 
to repeat myself here.

I don't have any ambitions of "declaring" things.  You can consider 
anything a conduct that you want and since wishing for artifacts is even 
declared one by the DevTeam who am I to object?  What I simply wanted to 
say is that I am not impressed by anyone who ascends a character with 
this as his only conduct.  I am impressed however by an ascension of a 
blind character or one that goes without food or without ever hitting 
with a wielded weapon.  I would be impressed by an ascension without 
magical resistance.  (Which I think is feasible, even with any starting 
character.  But it is better to choose one that does not have an 
MR-conferring quest artifact.)

